      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Follow up: According to my testing, Network.SetOwner blocks completely until either both parts of OnOwnershipRequest return true and all execution inside OnOwnershipTransferred is resolved OR when part 1 or 2 of OnOwnershipRequest returns false and the transfer is canceled.  Therefore, checking gameObject owner right after Network.SetOwner will indicate success or failure of the transfer.\nThe documentation explains that you should be able to safely call Network.SetOwner, change synced variables,  and call RequestSerialization in order and things should sync, but it doesn't explain by what mechanism it ensures that this works.  It would be nice for the docs to be updated with the information on the above process if it is correct.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "6178d7167522991d344db02b",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f2cc0dc3e5e4b3102c0e724",
