        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Upon further testing, changing synced variables directly after Network.SetOwner or inside OnOwnershipTransferred is NOT safe.  As of build 1144, some players will receive serialized data from the new owner BEFORE they receive the ownership transfer and discard it.  \nThis behavior is antithetical to manual sync, as the synced data will need to be periodically re-serialized to ensure its delivered.  Alternatively, every other player could use individually owned synced variables as semaphores to let a new owner know when they've all received ownership transfer and sync is reliable.  Both ways are dirty, and Udon networking should be changed to ensure that serialized data is received or at least processed after all ownership transfers for that object have been received.\nPossibly related to https://feedback.vrchat.com/udon-networking-update/p/1097-ownership-desync-issue\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-bugs/p/setting-ownership-to-someone-else-in-the-same-tick-as-requestserialization-cause",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
